{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1570453647,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MDM0NDA5NDU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3755","origin":"github"},"title":"create-sibling-github: Allow to specify {organization,login}/reponame","message":"A report came from our tireless pilot users, who tried `create-sibling-github hislogin/repo` to get `hislogin-repo` generated on github instead of expected `repo` under his `github.com/login`.  I think it would be nice from UX perspective to allow for `reponame` specification to carry `organization/` or `login/` prefix.  The tricky part on our side would be necessity to figure out, through interaction with github, either it is a login or organization since subsequent codepath is a bit different between the two, so it is not just a matter of splitting into `github_organization, reponame` as I have blindly tried first with \n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003ethis patch\u003c/summary\u003e \n\n```patch\ndiff --git a/datalad/distribution/create_sibling_github.py b/datalad/distribution/create_sibling_github.py\nindex fc8d74125..6b37da58c 100644\n--- a/datalad/distribution/create_sibling_github.py\n+++ b/datalad/distribution/create_sibling_github.py\n@@ -86,7 +86,9 @@ class CreateSiblingGithub(Interface):\n             args=('reponame',),\n             metavar='REPONAME',\n             doc=\"\"\"Github repository name. When operating recursively,\n-            a suffix will be appended to this name for each subdataset\"\"\",\n+            a suffix will be appended to this name for each subdataset. Could\n+            be used to specify both organization and repository name if\n+            specified as 'org/name'\"\"\",\n             constraints=EnsureStr()),\n         recursive=recursion_flag,\n         recursion_limit=recursion_limit,\n@@ -154,6 +156,16 @@ class CreateSiblingGithub(Interface):\n         # unnecessary dependencies\n         from datalad.support.github_ import _make_github_repos\n \n+        # If user provides \"login/repo\" (as they do), split based on '/'\n+        if '/' in reponame and not github_organization:\n+            github_organization, reponame_ = reponame.split('/', 1)\n+            lgr.info(\n+                \"Split original '%s' into '%s' organization and '%s' repo name\",\n+                reponame, github_organization, reponame_\n+            )\n+            reponame = reponame_\n+            del reponame_\n+\n         # what to operate on\n         ds = require_dataset(\n             dataset, check_installed=True, purpose='create Github sibling')\n```\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null}]}